# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Beihan Chen et al. (2025). Machine learning interatomic potential for predicting the thermal properties of uranium nitride.
#   Journal of Applied Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0294389  arXiv:2507.18786v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2507.18786v2 (sha256 6b81b4544cc7102f...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 381 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/chen2025predicting.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the VASP PBE+SOC (ferromagnetic, no Hubbard U) data
# set of 64-atom UN cells grown by MLIP-3 active learning with MD up to
# 3600 K (3,236 configurations, 90/10 train/validation), the MTP trained
# on it (energy, force and stress weights 0.85, 0.15, 0.001), and its
# validation RMSEs. Elastic constants, defect energies, thermal expansion,
# specific heat, melting point and thermal conductivity are properties.

